From d0165746ba526e8abae0b7cfa196c13f53621364 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:47:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Profiling: assembly of the prediction in the coupled
 organization

The assembly of the operator of the prediction (parallel assembly and
elimination of the essential degrees of freedom by FormLinearSystem) is
timed by the section PRED::assemble without the kernels too, as with
them: it was counted in NLEPIB::computePrediction only.
---
 src/NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementation.cxx | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementation.cxx b/src/NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementation.cxx
index 4c0dd87326..617281b871 100644
--- a/src/NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementation.cxx
+++ b/src/NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementation.cxx
@@ -880,6 +880,11 @@ namespace mfem_mgis {
         return registerExceptionInErrorBacktrace(ctx);
       }
     } else {
+      // the assembly of the operator of the prediction (parallel assembly
+      // and elimination of the essential degrees of freedom; the element
+      // matrices are computed in `PRED::forms` here, in `PRED::assemble`
+      // with the kernels)
+      CatchTimeSection(ctx, "PRED::assemble");
       // diagonal set to one at the essential degrees of freedom, as in
       // parallel and with the kernels (the sequential bilinear forms of MFEM
       // keep the diagonal of the stiffness by default): an iterative linear
